    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557">

                <pb facs="1004" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4988: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-02">February 2,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>828. Concerning assistance to Danish refugees now in Sweden referred to in your
                    303 January 12,<anchor n="27" xml:id="d557-f1"/> Department concurs with views
                    as expressed by British Foreign Office. In collaboration with the British please
                    refer matter to IGC requesting it to coordinate all activities in consultation
                    with our Governments, the Swedish Government and the Danish Ministers in
                    Washington and London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d557-f1" n="27" xml:id="d557-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it contained the text of a letter of January 10 from the British
                    Foreign Office with respect to refugees from Denmark in Sweden, requesting that
                    an inquiry be made of the State Department whether they would agree that the
                    organization of aid to these refugees should be entrusted to the
                    Intergovernmental Committee who would be enabled to coordinate all activities in
                    consultation with the United States and British Governments and with the Swedish
                    Government and the recognized Danish authorities (840.48 Refugees/4988).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
